Package: com.supremeinspirit.nomoreuselessactivity
Name: NoMoreUselessActivity
Version: 1.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64
Section: Tweaks
Maintainer: supremeinspirit
Author: supremeinspirit
Depends: firmware (>= 15.0), mobilesubstrate
Description: Stops system daemons from burning CPU in the background for nothing (the "KeySpinFix"). What it fixes: on a jailbroken phone UIKit gets loaded into background daemons (Siri, Focus, Wallet, Screen Time, photo conversion and others). When such a daemon is told that it "entered the background", UIKit's keyboard code (UIKeyboardInputModeController) tries to hop to the main thread first. A daemon has no real main thread, so the hop is repeated without end: the daemon does nothing useful and still keeps a CPU core busy, for days, until it is killed. This tweak drops those calls in everything that is not an app or an app extension; apps and the keyboard itself are not touched, and there are no settings. What it means for the CPU cores, measured on an iPhone 15 Pro Max (iOS 17.3, Dopamine): 13 daemons each held about 20 % of an efficiency core nonstop, together roughly three full cores of pure waste (whole system about 400 % of one core, load average about 16), so the efficiency cores never went to sleep and everything else had to share what was left. With the fix the same daemons sit at 0.0 % (0.6 to 12 seconds of CPU time in two hours instead of about 3000 seconds each), the whole system dropped to about 85 % of one core with an app in front and the load average to about 6. In practice: the cores can idle again, the phone stays cooler and the battery drains clearly slower. If your phone does not have this spin, the tweak changes nothing. A daemon gets the fix when it next starts, so reboot userspace (or reboot and re-jailbreak) after installing. Tested on that one device only; rootless, A12 or newer device.
